From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reindert Pelsma <reindert.pelsma@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 17:10:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] accel/kvm: retry a bare KVM_RUN EFAULT instead of
 killing the VM

An NVIDIA GPU mapping is VM_IO|VM_PFNMAP, and the driver's fault handler
(nv_fault(), kernel-open/nvidia/nv-mmap.c) has two paths that return
VM_FAULT_NOPAGE *without* installing a PTE -- the PM-lock trylock failing,
and !nvl->safe_to_mmap while a GPU wakeup is scheduled.  Both mean "come
back later".  A userspace process honours that by re-faulting; KVM calls
fixup_user_fault() once, still finds no PTE, and returns a bare -EFAULT,
which QEMU has always treated as fatal.  The guest therefore dies on a
mapping that was about to be reinstated.

RIP has not advanced when KVM_RUN returns, so re-entering the guest simply
re-executes the same access.  This retries a bare EFAULT (i.e. one that is
NOT a KVM_EXIT_MEMORY_FAULT, which has its own handling) on a 3 s budget in
5 ms steps, logs once on entry and once on exit, and falls through to the
original fatal path if it never clears.

The budget is measured, not guessed: on the RTX 3050 laptop the fault
cleared after 1465 ms.  An earlier attempt used 64 x 200us -- about 13 ms
total -- and concluded from that that the fault was permanent, which is why
the number is this large and why it is expressed in milliseconds against a
GPU wakeup rather than as a spin count.

This patch had no commit message before the 9.2 -> 11.1 rebase (the file in
patches/ was a bare diff with no mail header); the rationale above is
recovered from the in-code comment and patches/README.md.
---
 accel/kvm/kvm-all.c | 49 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 49 insertions(+)

diff --git a/accel/kvm/kvm-all.c b/accel/kvm/kvm-all.c
index 83cbd120a8..1300c861bc 100644
--- a/accel/kvm/kvm-all.c
+++ b/accel/kvm/kvm-all.c
@@ -3424,8 +3424,13 @@ out_unref:
     return ret;
 }
 
+/* nvkvm: how long to keep retrying a bare KVM_RUN EFAULT; see the use site. */
+#define NVKVM_EFAULT_BUDGET_MS 3000
+#define NVKVM_EFAULT_STEP_MS   5
+
 int kvm_cpu_exec(CPUState *cpu)
 {
+    int nvkvm_efault_ms = 0;
     struct kvm_run *run = cpu->kvm_run;
     int ret, run_ret;
 
@@ -3490,6 +3495,44 @@ int kvm_cpu_exec(CPUState *cpu)
                 break;
             }
             if (!(run_ret == -EFAULT && run->exit_reason == KVM_EXIT_MEMORY_FAULT)) {
+                /*
+                 * nvkvm: a bare KVM_RUN EFAULT is "come back later", not death.
+                 *
+                 * KVM resolves a memslot HVA through hva_to_pfn_remapped() for
+                 * a VM_IO|VM_PFNMAP VMA -- an NVIDIA GPU mapping.  The driver's
+                 * fault handler (nv_fault, kernel-open/nvidia/nv-mmap.c) has two
+                 * paths that return VM_FAULT_NOPAGE *without* installing a PTE:
+                 *
+                 *   if (!down_read_trylock(&nv_system_pm_lock))  -> NOPAGE
+                 *   if (!nvl->safe_to_mmap) { rm_schedule_gpu_wakeup(); NOPAGE; }
+                 *
+                 * Both mean "retry, the mapping is coming".  A userspace process
+                 * honours that by re-faulting.  KVM calls fixup_user_fault()
+                 * once, still finds no PTE via follow_pte(), and returns -EFAULT,
+                 * which QEMU has always treated as fatal -- so the guest dies on
+                 * a mapping that was about to be reinstated.
+                 *
+                 * RIP has not advanced when KVM_RUN returns, so re-entering the
+                 * guest simply re-executes the same access.  Retry on a budget
+                 * measured against a GPU wakeup (hundreds of ms), not a spinloop:
+                 * an earlier 64 x 200us attempt covered ~13ms and concluded,
+                 * wrongly, that the fault was permanent.
+                 */
+                if (run_ret == -EFAULT &&
+                    nvkvm_efault_ms < NVKVM_EFAULT_BUDGET_MS) {
+                    if (nvkvm_efault_ms == 0) {
+                        fprintf(stderr, "nvkvm: KVM_RUN EFAULT -- mapping not "
+                                "resolvable yet, retrying up to %d ms\n",
+                                NVKVM_EFAULT_BUDGET_MS);
+                    }
+                    g_usleep(NVKVM_EFAULT_STEP_MS * 1000);
+                    nvkvm_efault_ms += NVKVM_EFAULT_STEP_MS;
+                    continue;
+                }
+                if (run_ret == -EFAULT) {
+                    fprintf(stderr, "nvkvm: KVM_RUN EFAULT persisted for %d ms "
+                            "-- giving up\n", nvkvm_efault_ms);
+                }
                 fprintf(stderr, "error: kvm run failed %s\n",
                         strerror(-run_ret));
 #ifdef TARGET_PPC
@@ -3505,6 +3548,12 @@ int kvm_cpu_exec(CPUState *cpu)
             }
         }
 
+        if (nvkvm_efault_ms) {
+            fprintf(stderr, "nvkvm: KVM_RUN EFAULT cleared after %d ms\n",
+                    nvkvm_efault_ms);
+            nvkvm_efault_ms = 0;   /* nvkvm: forward progress */
+        }
+
         trace_kvm_run_exit(cpu->cpu_index, run->exit_reason);
         switch (run->exit_reason) {
         case KVM_EXIT_IO:
